{"id": "whhortobagy", "name": "Hortobágy National Park - the Puszta", "short": "Hortobágy", "place": "Hungary", "lat": 47.6, "lon": 21.1, "side": "r", "cont": "Europe", "country": "Hungary", "kind": "Grassland", "park": true, "blurb": "Alkaline puszta where grazing herds, ground squirrels and falcons share open steppe.", "tip": {"id": "gsq", "title": "Remove the ground squirrels", "text": "Ground squirrels feed saker falcons and foxes. Set European ground squirrel to -100% and watch the saker falcon, then foxes turning to other prey such as bustards."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Hortobágy National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hortob%C3%A1gy_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage: Hortobágy National Park - the Puszta", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/474/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Great bustard", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_bustard"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: European ground squirrel", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_ground_squirrel"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Common crane", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_crane"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Saker falcon", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saker_falcon"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Hortobágy National Park", "icon": "grass", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Summer sun powers the open, treeless grassland and the shallow wetlands that make up the puszta."}, {"id": "alk", "sp": "alkaline soils", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "tisza", "sp": "tisza river floods", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "wet", "sp": "marshes and fishponds", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "decomposers", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "Fungi, bacteria and soil invertebrates break down dung, dead grass and carcasses and return nutrients to the soil."}, {"id": "grass", "sp": "festuca", "xh": 0.25, "name": "Puszta grasses", "desc": "Short, hardy grasses and herbs of the alkaline pastures; they feed the grazers and are kept short by them."}, {"id": "reed", "sp": "phragmites australis", "xh": 0.55, "wiki": "Phragmites", "desc": "Reed beds line the marshes and fishponds, giving food and cover to geese, herons and harriers."}, {"id": "cress", "sp": "lepidium draba", "xh": 0.8}, {"id": "cattle", "sp": "bos taurus", "xh": 0.05, "name": "Hungarian Grey cattle", "wiki": "Hungarian Grey cattle", "desc": "A hardy landrace long herded on the puszta by mounted csikos. Grazing keeps the pasture open and short.", "ic": "bison", "badge": "Keystone grazer"}, {"id": "horse", "sp": "equus ferus", "xh": 0.17}, {"id": "gsq", "sp": "spermophilus citellus", "xh": 0.29}, {"id": "hamster", "sp": "cricetus cricetus", "xh": 0.41}, {"id": "maniola", "sp": "maniola jurtina", "xh": 0.53}, {"id": "goose", "sp": "anser anser", "xh": 0.65}, {"id": "crane", "sp": "grus grus", "xh": 0.77}, {"id": "bustard", "sp": "otis tarda", "xh": 0.89}, {"id": "frog", "sp": "pelophylax ridibundus", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "A large water frog of ponds and canals that eats insects and other small animals and is food for herons, snakes and eagles.", "ic": "quad"}, {"id": "snake", "sp": "natrix natrix", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "heron", "sp": "ardea cinerea", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "A wading bird that spears frogs, snakes and small mammals at the edges of fishponds and in wet grassland."}, {"id": "harrier", "sp": "circus aeruginosus", "xh": 0.7, "tl": 3, "desc": "A raptor of reed beds that hunts frogs, snakes and small mammals over wetlands and nearby fields."}, {"id": "fox", "sp": "vulpes vulpes", "xh": 0.9, "wiki": "Red fox", "desc": "A generalist that takes rodents, ground squirrels, birds and their eggs, frogs and carrion."}, {"id": "saker", "sp": "falco cherrug", "xh": 0.3}, {"id": "eagle", "sp": "haliaeetus albicilla", "xh": 0.7, "desc":